    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pax was incorporated in 1920 and named for Pack's Branch, a tributary of Paint Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/travel/communities/cities-towns/pax-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before becoming Pax, this community was first known as Paintsville due to its location on Paint Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/travel/communities/cities-towns/pax-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coal mining boomed in the region as railroads opened, which greatly supported the growth and commerce of Pax.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/travel/communities/cities-towns/pax-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Burial mounds, petroglyphs, and other earthworks have been found throughout the immediate area of Pax.",
